comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T14:23:58.574Z","harness:claude-code","Scope input 2026-07-31 from pm-aka8m7. This chore consolidates the load, verify, rewrite, re-anchor, report pipeline across redact, repair and compact, and that consolidation is the right and only place to add one thing all three paths currently omit.\n\nreanchorHistoryEntries at src/core/history/replay.ts:365-370 overwrites before_hash and after_hash in place and retains the prior values nowhere - the result carries an entriesRehashed count and a per-entry rehashed boolean. Every one of the three commands this chore unifies therefore destroys the anchors its inputs committed to, and so does every union merge, since src/sdk/merge/three-way.ts:57 documents reanchored as true for every union. Adding retention per command would mean writing it three times and would leave the merge driver's own path a fourth; adding it at the unified pipeline covers all four at once.\n\nRecommend widening this chore's acceptance criteria to include the retention hook - the shared pipeline emits the original anchor pair for each rewritten entry to whichever durable sink the owning command chooses - without taking on the storage-location decision, which belongs to pm-aka8m7. That keeps this chore mechanical while making the fix a one-site change afterwards rather than a four-site one."
  "2026-09-07T09:09:45.363Z","harness:codex","Implementation scope: complete all-status CLI read returned 2653 items with complete receipt, no omissions, no unreadable records. Reuse existing maintenance lineage with pm-tqel; no new duplicate. Current source already retains reanchor evidence and CLI copy/restore are SDK reexports. Consolidate remaining subject resolution, consistent input snapshots, transform verification and guarded application while preserving operation-specific reconciliation, privacy, checkpoint and rollback semantics. GitHub initial inventory: zero open PRs, issues, Dependabot alerts and code-scanning alerts; three latest auto-release runs succeeded."
  "2026-09-07T09:45:05.663Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: shared stream snapshot and verified maintenance pipeline integrated with redact/repair/compact and restore drift checks. Native history commands share registrations with permanent root aliases; runtime flags, output envelopes, addressing, SDK/MCP discovery and completion resolve the selected operation. Focused maintenance and namespace suites passed; full coverage and type gates are running."
  "2026-09-07T09:52:27.953Z","harness:codex","Verification progress: full source typechecking, repository ESLint, zero-clone duplicate gates, public documentation links and flag invocation parity passed. The command-grammar run overlapped a test-wrapper rebuild and observed one transient module-export failure; help succeeds on the settled build and the grammar gate is being rerun without overlapping builds. SDK surface generation also identified the required aggregate re-exports for the new history alias contracts; those are now added."
  "2026-09-07T10:07:09.045Z","harness:codex","Verification progress: 71 focused command and SDK regression tests passed after native history addressing and contract fixes. SDK surface refresh records additive optional omission metadata and the equivalent PmSettings signature. The stricter 12-line/60-token history scan identified a remaining workspace initialization clone and a settled event-index opening clone; both now share typed helpers without changing lock order or error ownership. Full coverage and repository assurance are running; these are not yet final green claims."
  "2026-09-07T10:11:29.194Z","harness:codex","Gate migration rationale: five direct workspace initialization guards now call one shared resolver. The direct-call ratchet moves from 50 to the observed 47, while a new minimum of five resolver delegations and explicit per-file parity contracts protect all five maintenance entrypoints plus the shared assertion. Added real uninitialized-workspace rejection coverage for redact, repair, repair-all, compact and compact-bulk. No initialization refusal was removed."
  "2026-09-07T10:48:12.031Z","harness:codex","Final local verification passed: all 8536 tests in 636 files; exact coverage 63186/63186 statements, 47977/47977 branches, 13105/13105 functions and 60680/60680 lines. All three linked verification commands passed, including the stricter 12-line/60-token history duplicate scan. Final build, ESLint, contract/generated snapshots, SDK surface, repository assurance, command/refusal/token/parity gates, graph composition and record integrity passed. Import and transport benchmarks passed in isolation after a CPU-contended run. No coverage exclusions, thresholds or timing budgets were relaxed."
  "2026-09-07T11:21:20.355Z","harness:codex","Review correction: title now describes the completed shared SDK pipeline so package-generated release notes do not repeat the original defect as current architecture. Preserve the detailed original problem statement and immutable resolution/history. Added purpose documentation to touched internal event-index, repair, redaction, compaction and restore helpers; no maintenance policy or thresholds changed."
  "2026-09-07T11:32:58.931Z","harness:codex","Review fixes verified: final 8537-test suite passed with exact 100/100/100/100 and zero uncovered counts; all three linked verification commands passed, including the strict history duplicate scan. Completed shared-pipeline title and purpose docstrings preserve historical problem/evidence records. Final tracked-source static gate passed, and installed npm/Bun redaction, restoration, compaction, chain verification and SDK execution passed again."
  "2026-09-07T12:29:14.462Z","harness:codex","Review documentation follow-up: transaction callbacks now explain locked rewrite ownership, coupled rollback, abandonment proof checks, privacy-safe reports and restore decoding. Full final suite passed all 8538 tests with exact 100/100/100/100; rebuilt npm and Bun candidates passed 15-step history journeys, public SDK execution and six additional sensitive-recovery cases each. A temporary-host inode exhaustion interrupted one Bun install; removing only this session disposable dependency folders resolved it, and the rerun passed."
  "2026-09-07T12:33:23.088Z","harness:codex","Final review correction verified: all 8538 tests in 637 files passed with exact 100/100/100/100 and zero uncovered counts. Final build, full quality:static chain and both linked namespace commands passed. Installed npm and Bun each passed 15 history workflow steps, public SDK execution and six option-shaped sensitive-recovery cases. Actual Zsh execution verifies all five native mappings with correct CURRENT positions; the proposed offset change is a false positive. Purpose documentation now includes maintenance callbacks; restore docs accept timestamp-or-version. Every completed-review artifact and edited revision has a reaction and contextual acknowledgement. Updated-head hosted checks and full review remain separate before merge."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-07T10:43:14.796Z","harness:codex",Read stream bytes and decoded entries in one snapshot before planning. A second independent read can bind a rewrite to different source bytes; item and stream drift must both be rechecked under the existing write lock.
